---
name: test-driven-development
description: Use for behavior-changing features and bug fixes where a regression test can capture the contract. Avoid for pure configuration, documentation, generated files, or tests that only restate wiring.
---

# Test-driven development

For a behavior change, state the consumer-visible behavior and boundary case first. Add or identify a deterministic test that would fail for the missing behavior. For a reproducible bug, confirm the regression test fails for the reported reason before fixing it; do not rerun a failure the user has already reported as ground truth.

Implement the smallest change that passes the test. Run the focused test, then the broader relevant suite when appropriate. Refactor only while the tests remain green. If a failing-first test is impractical, use a direct scenario/smoke check and say so; do not add tautological tests for forwarding, copies, or incidental defaults.
